==Special Moves==
====Hangetsu Zan====
{{FrameDataCargo-COTW
|moveId=kim_214b,kim_214d,kim_214bd
|input=214B/D/BD
|input2=qcb+B/D/BD
|description3=Kaphwan does a somersaulting crescent kick.
* All versions hit from round start distance and go over certain lows. They also hit OTG
* Unlike Jae Hoon, Kaphwan cannot brake any version
This versatile special move defines Kaphwan as a character. The Hangetsu Zan is a combo ender, punish tool, advancing move, and more all rolled into one, though each version has its own uses.
----
'''Light version (214B)''': A versatile tool that can be used in a bunch of different ways.
* Combos from lights
* Always knocks down on hit, unlike the other two versions
* Launches on Counter Hit, making it one of Kaphwan’s strongest punishes on DPs and whiffed REV Blows
* Good as a poke if you space it properly; its pushback on block is much worse than other games
----
'''Heavy version (214D)''': High risk, but high return. 
* Leaves standing on grounded hit, giving a combo to 2C on Wild Punish
* Kaphwan’s optimal OTG after a sweep that Wild Punishes
----
'''REV version (214BD)''': The ultimate round-start jumpscare, reminiscent of KOF XIII. Gets Kaphwan in their face quickly and lets him push more offense with REV Accel.
* Retains almost all of 214D’s properties, but has faster startup and is safer on block
}}

====Hien Zan====
{{FrameDataCargo-COTW
|moveId=kim_28b,kim_28d,kim_28bd,kim_28d_6d,kim_28bd_6d,
|input=[2]8B/D/BD
|input2=[d]u+B/D/BD
|description5=Kaphwan’s flashkick.
* ~40f charge time for all versions
* All versions have invincibility to air attacks on startup
* Like all anti-air specials, all versions are Counter Hit punishable on recovery if Kaphwan doesn’t brake them
One of Kaphwan’s other defining specials, an anti-air kick. This is a charge move, which carries both benefits (like reaction punishes) and downsides (like having to charge it). Nonetheless, it is important to Kaphwan’s defense and combos alike. Knowing which version to use, and when, is key to playing the character at his best. 
----
'''Light version ([2]8B)''': Kaphwan’s main invincible reversal, and his fastest special move overall. 
* Fully invincible on startup
* Cannot be braked nor cancelled to the follow-up, making it extremely punishable
* Quick enough to tack on at the end of his Command Combos or various juggles
----
'''Heavy version ([2]8D)''': Kaphwan’s main anti-air. 
* Launches on hit, safe on block. Your optimal resourceless combo is 236B > [2]8B
* Only the second hit launches on Counter Hit
* Can be followed up with a second kick if you don’t brake it, input with 6D
----
'''REV version ([2]8BD)'''
* Nearly identical properties to the Heavy version, right down to the startup, damage and optional follow-up
* Launches higher when braked than the heavy version, enabling unique juggles
}}

====Hishou Kyaku====
{{FrameDataCargo-COTW
|moveId=kim_j.236b,kim_j.236d,kim_j.236bd
|input=j.236B/D/BD
|input2=j.qcf+B/D/BD
|description3=A multi-hitting divekick that functions wholly differently depending on the version used. 
* All versions can be done from a forward or neutral jump, and can be done surprisingly low to the ground
* Kaphwan briefly stalls in the air before divekicking, allowing them to bait and punish certain anti-airs (such as High Dodge Attacks)
* Frame advantages on Counter Hit / Wild Punish do not carry over past the first hit
This divekick's main use is for baiting anti-airs or to punish the opponent from a neutral jump. It means Kaphwan doesn't appear to give up as much space by neutral jumping than he appears. 
----
'''Light version (236B)''': Kaphwan kicks the opponent in the face repeatedly.
* The damage is pretty decent, but the okizeme is not
* Horrendous on block, even with the backward bounce
* Combos from j.A on Counter Hit, or j.214D brake on normal hit
----
'''Heavy version (236D)''': Kaphwan keeps kicking downward until he lands.
* Safe, but finnicky on hit and block
* On grounded hit or block, Kaphwan will always land in throw range
* If you Counter Hit or Wild Punish a grounded opponent with the first hit ONLY, Kaphwan can link 2A or far A to pick up a combo
